ollama (0.33.3) stable; urgency=medium

  The package now installs changelog, NEWS.Debian, and upstream NEWS
  files in /usr/share/doc/ollama/. Users who install apt-listchanges
  will see upgrade notes before each upgrade:

    apt install apt-listchanges

  These files provide:
  - changelog.gz - Full Debian changelog history
  - NEWS.Debian.gz - Significant packaging changes (this file)
  - NEWS.gz - Upstream ollama release notes

 -- lingfish <lingfish@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 03 Sep 2026 16:41:00 +1000

ollama (0.30.8+repack1) stable; urgency=medium

  The ollama APT repository now provides a main component containing
  only libre packages (ollama and libollama-common) for use on
  free-software-only systems such as Trisquel.

  Users on Trisquel or other free systems should use the main component
  instead of non-free:

    deb https://lingfish.github.io/ollama-deb/apt stable main

  Users on standard Debian/Ubuntu systems should continue using non-free
  to get GPU backend packages:

    deb https://lingfish.github.io/ollama-deb/apt stable non-free

  The ollama package has been split into multiple packages to better
  support different GPU configurations:

    ollama                  - Main program (required)
    libollama-common        - CPU dispatch and Vulkan libraries (required)
    libollama-nvidia        - NVIDIA CUDA backend (install for NVIDIA GPUs)
    libollama-amd           - AMD ROCm backend (install for AMD GPUs)

  APT will suggest the appropriate GPU backend package during install.
  To install with NVIDIA support:

    apt install ollama libollama-nvidia

  To install with AMD support:

    apt install ollama libollama-amd

  The ollama user is now automatically added to the render and video
  groups for GPU access.

 -- lingfish <lingfish@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 01 Sep 2026 06:07:29 +0000
